ok - a recycled pid does not read as the lock holder
    (a pid reused by an unrelated process -> mismatch, NOT held, reclaimed)
ok - a recorded holder with no process left is reclaimed
ok - an identity that cannot be re-proved keeps the lock with the holder
ok - a lock with no recorded identity is never stolen, and says so
    (the permissive upgrade-window rule for pre-existing locks)

